{"vul":143,"heb":144,"title":"Psalmus David. Adversus Goliath.","incipit":"Benedictus Dominus","verses":[{"n":1,"la":["Benedictus","Dominus","Deus","meus,","qui","docet","manus","meas","ad","prælium,","et","digitos","meos","ad","bellum."],"gl":["blessed","Lord","God","my","who","teaches","hands","my","for","battle","and","fingers","my","for","war"],"en":"Blessed be the Lord my God, who teacheth my hands to fight, and my fingers to war."},{"n":2,"la":["Misericordia","mea","et","refugium","meum;","susceptor","meus","et","liberator","meus;","protector","meus,","et","in","ipso","speravi,","qui","subdit","populum","meum","sub","me."],"gl":["mercy","my","and","refuge","my","upholder","my","and","deliverer","my","protector","my","and","in","him","I hoped","who","subdues","people","my","under","me"],"en":"My mercy, and my refuge: my support, and my deliverer: My protector, and I have hoped in him: who subdueth my people under me."},{"n":3,"la":["Domine,","quid","est","homo,","quia","innotuisti","ei?","aut","filius","hominis,","quia","reputas","eum?"],"gl":["O Lord","what","is","man","that","you made known","to him","or","son","of man","that","you regard","him"],"en":"Lord, what is man, that thou art made known to him? or the son of man, that thou makest account of him?"},{"n":4,"la":["Homo","vanitati","similis","factus","est;","dies","ejus","sicut","umbra","prætereunt."],"gl":["man","to vanity","like","made","is","days","his","like","shadow","pass away"],"en":"Man is like to vanity: his days pass away like a shadow."},{"n":5,"la":["Domine,","inclina","cælos","tuos,","et","descende;","tange","montes,","et","fumigabunt."],"gl":["O Lord","bow","heavens","your","and","come down","touch","mountains","and","they will smoke"],"en":"Lord, bow down thy heavens and descend: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke."},{"n":6,"la":["Fulgura","coruscationem,","et","dissipabis","eos;","emitte","sagittas","tuas,","et","conturbabis","eos."],"gl":["flash forth","lightning","and","you will scatter","them","send out","arrows","your","and","you will confound","them"],"en":"Send forth lightning, and thou shalt scatter them: shoot out thy arrows, and thou shalt trouble them."},{"n":7,"la":["Emitte","manum","tuam","de","alto:","eripe","me,","et","libera","me","de","aquis","multis,","de","manu","filiorum","alienorum:"],"gl":["stretch out","hand","your","from","on high","snatch","me","and","free","me","from","waters","many","from","hand","of sons","foreign"],"en":"Put forth thy hand from on high, take me out, and deliver me from many waters: from the hand of strange children:"},{"n":8,"la":["quorum","os","locutum","est","vanitatem,","et","dextera","eorum","dextera","iniquitatis."],"gl":["whose","mouth","spoken","has","vanity","and","right hand","their","right hand","of iniquity"],"en":"Whose mouth hath spoken vanity: and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity."},{"n":9,"la":["Deus,","canticum","novum","cantabo","tibi;","in","psalterio","decachordo","psallam","tibi."],"gl":["O God","song","new","I will sing","to you","on","psaltery","ten-stringed","I will play","to you"],"en":"To thee, O God, I will sing a new canticle: on the psaltery and an instrument of ten strings I will sing praises to thee."},{"n":10,"la":["Qui","das","salutem","regibus,","qui","redemisti","David","servum","tuum","de","gladio","maligno,"],"gl":["who","give","salvation","to kings","who","redeemed","David","servant","your","from","sword","evil"],"en":"Who givest salvation to kings: who hast redeemed thy servant David from the malicious sword:"},{"n":11,"la":["eripe","me,","et","erue","me","de","manu","filiorum","alienorum,","quorum","os","locutum","est","vanitatem,","et","dextera","eorum","dextera","iniquitatis."],"gl":["snatch","me","and","pluck","me","from","hand","of sons","foreign","whose","mouth","spoken","has","vanity","and","right hand","their","right hand","of iniquity"],"en":"Deliver me, And rescue me out of the hand of strange children; whose mouth hath spoken vanity: and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity:"},{"n":12,"la":["Quorum","filii","sicut","novellæ","plantationes","in","juventute","sua;","filiæ","eorum","compositæ,","circumornatæ","ut","similitudo","templi."],"gl":["whose","sons","like","young","plantings","in","youth","their","daughters","their","adorned","decked about","as","likeness","of temple"],"en":"Whose sons are as new plants in their youth: Their daughters decked out, adorned round about after the similitude of a temple:"},{"n":13,"la":["Promptuaria","eorum","plena,","eructantia","ex","hoc","in","illud;","oves","eorum","fœtosæ,","abundantes","in","egressibus","suis;"],"gl":["storehouses","their","full","overflowing","from","this","into","that","sheep","their","fruitful","abounding","in","goings-out","their"],"en":"Their storehouses full, flowing out of this into that. Their sheep fruitful in young, abounding in their goings forth:"},{"n":14,"la":["boves","eorum","crassæ.","Non","est","ruina","maceriæ,","neque","transitus,","neque","clamor","in","plateis","eorum."],"gl":["oxen","their","fat","not","is","breach","of wall","nor","passage","nor","outcry","in","streets","their"],"en":"their oxen fat. There is no breach of wall, nor passage, nor crying out in their streets."},{"n":15,"la":["Beatum","dixerunt","populum","cui","hæc","sunt;","beatus","populus","cujus","Dominus","Deus","ejus."],"gl":["happy","they called","people","to whom","these things","are","happy","people","whose","Lord","God","its"],"en":"They have called the people happy, that hath these things: but happy is that people whose God is the Lord."}]}